    "method": {
      "names_own_assignment": "speaker's own assigned entity appears in the message. UNINFORMATIVE: the assigned entities are the answer options, so this is ~1.0 under both conditions and measures 'discusses the candidates', not disclosure. Reported because its symmetry across conditions is the evidence for that.",
      "standing_claim": "first-person claim of standing ('my review', 'I was assigned', 'assigned to me'). This is the disclosure measure.",
      "standing_claim_linked_to_own": "a standing claim in the SAME CLAUSE as the speaker's own assigned entity, with no other candidate intervening; the strongest literal evidence a reader could identify the speaker's assignment from content alone. Precision 99.0% (Wilson 95% CI 96.4-99.7) on 200 randomly sampled flagged clauses labelled by hand.",
      "standing_claim_linked_proximity": "superseded: the same claim within 120 characters, which crosses sentence and clause boundaries. Retained only so the two can be compared.",
      "frozen_verifier_round1_anonymous_distinct_wordings": "the same rows deduplicated on wording. The verifier message is generated once and replayed across the delivery arms, so the raw bucket counts one wording several times; this is the rate per distinct message and the one to quote.",
      "bound": "all are lower bounds; paraphrase is not matched"
    },
